From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:53:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] editor brush: native shaped terrain brush (shape masks
 uploaded once, bilinear read with the turn), shaped weights for the erosion
 brush

ed_brush_shape_set(handle, n, values) stores an n x n mask over the unit square; ed_terrain_brush takes a shape handle and an angle (arguments 13, 14) and the mask
replaces the falloff profile with the maths of brushes.lua Weight (u,v turned by the angle, bilinear read, 0 beyond 1.6 and the radius). ed_erode_dab takes opts.shape /
opts.angle and builds the window weights natively instead of from a Lua list. Tests: shaped dabs against the float Lua transliteration (word for word) and a double
reference, orientation, registry, FillShapeWeights, a 64-radius benchmark.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F37er45a7etRuMgEW1q3kY

